        "MapML-MapLibre": {
          "passed": 4,
          "failed": 0,
          "flaky": 0,
          "skipped": 4,
          "build": "cross-port-tests@c6aa2d8+dirty",
          "date": "2026-11-01"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Runs in OSMTILE and CBMTILE (@CBMTILE); MapML-MapLibre skips the CBMTILE run. Each test builds its own viewer; the locate button is found through the locate-control testid instead of its English title; locate() results are polled for instead of read straight away / after waitForTimeout. The OSMTILE run uses tiles/osmtile/osmtile-z18.mapml: the map's zoom range is its layers', so locate()'s zoom 16 needs a layer that reaches it (as upstream's cbmt.mapml, 0-17, does). Upstream's locationerror test dispatched the event itself, testing no implementation; it now withdraws the geolocation permission so locate() really fails. The button test also checks that locate() turns location tracking off, as MapML.js does (GeolocationButton.stop()). MapML-MapLibre's locate() left tracking on and was changed to stop it; MapML-OpenLayers and MapML-MapLibre were changed to limit the map's zoom range to their layers' as MapML.js does (setMapMinAndMaxZoom), which no converted spec asserts yet. MapML-OpenLayers test/locate.test.js stays pending: its button tests belong to mapml-viewer/locateButton.test.js.",
      "supersedes": {
        "MapML-MapLibre": [
          "tests/locate-api.spec.ts"
        ]
      }
    },
